// Audit §7.1: the loop's `}` and the enclosing block's `}` are on the SAME
// line, so the `while` is the block's last statement with no newline between
// the two braces. A value-less loop is a statement, never the block's tail
// expression: before the fix the parser promoted it and the emitter raised
// "internal: stack imbalance in expression Block: expected height 1,
// emitter computed 0" on this legal program. The condition is false, so the
// loop body never runs.
// EXPECT: start
fn main() {
    print("start")
    while false { print("never") } }
